course: dictionary
lesson: 12571
title: Diluted: made weaker
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Diluted means made weaker or thinner, usually by adding water or another liquid. Context helps you find its meaning. «Mum poured the squash and added water until it was diluted.» Adding water makes squash weaker and less strong, so diluted fits.
explain: The word can also mean weaker in effect, not just in taste. «The school's new rule was a diluted version of the first plan.» The rule was not gone, but it was softer and less strong than the original. Always check: swap in weaker and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Diluted is the past form of dilute. You can see the family: dilute, dilutes, diluting, diluted. The ending tells you the time. «Sam dilutes the juice» happens now, but «Sam diluted the juice» happened earlier.
fact: Diluted means made weaker or thinner, often by adding water.
fact: «Diluted» is the past form of the verb dilute.
fact: «The juice is diluted with water» means water has been added to it.
fact: A diluted solution is less concentrated than the strong version it came from.
fact: Phrases you may see: «watered-down» means made weaker, and «a diluted plan» means a weaker version of the first plan.
exercise: «The orange drink was diluted with lots of water.» What does diluted mean here? | Frozen solid | Poured very slowly | *Made weaker by adding water | Made stronger by adding sugar
exercise: Ben says the school rule was a «diluted version» of the first plan. What does that suggest? | *The rule was weaker than the first plan | The rule was made of water | The rule was stronger than the first plan | The rule was thrown away
exercise: Which word is the past form of dilute? | dilute | dilutes | diluting | *diluted
test: «The bleach was well diluted before we used it to clean the sink.» What does well diluted mean? | *Mixed with a lot of water, so it was weaker | Very thick and strong | Left out in the sun | Heated until it boils
test: «His watered-down apology did not sound sincere.» What does watered-down suggest? | Very loud and long | Made of real water | *Made weaker and less strong | Spoken in a new language
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to diluted when we talk about squash with extra water added? | *Weakened | Sweetened | Frozen | Thickened
